  "id": "illusory-movement",
  "term": "illusory movement",
  "definition": "Illusory movement is the experience of seeing motion in a visual stimulus even though the movement is not physically present. In the described context, this perceived motion can be tracked with the eyes and can support smooth pursuit in different directions.",
